language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Magic hexagon: arrange the numbers 1 to NUM_CELLS in the hexagon cells A to S so that the numbers in each of the 15 lines (rows and diagonals) add up to the magic constant.
given NUM_CELLS : int
given MAGIC_SUM : int
find LD : matrix indexed by [int(1..NUM_CELLS)] of int(1..NUM_CELLS)

branching on [LD]
such that
$ every cell holds a different number
allDiff(LD),
$ the five horizontal lines ABC, DEFG, HIJKL, MNOP and QRS each sum to the magic constant
LD[1] + LD[2] + LD[3] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[4] + LD[5] + LD[6] + LD[7] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[8] + LD[9] + LD[10] + LD[11] + LD[12] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[13] + LD[14] + LD[15] + LD[16] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[17] + LD[18] + LD[19] = MAGIC_SUM,
$ the lines running down and to the right, AEJOS, BFKP, CGL, DINR and HMQ, each sum to the magic constant
LD[1] + LD[5] + LD[10] + LD[15] + LD[19] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[2] + LD[6] + LD[11] + LD[16] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[3] + LD[7] + LD[12] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[4] + LD[9] + LD[14] + LD[18] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[8] + LD[13] + LD[17] = MAGIC_SUM,
$ the lines running down and to the left, ADH, BEIM, CFJNQ, GKOR and LPS, each sum to the magic constant
LD[1] + LD[4] + LD[8] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[2] + LD[5] + LD[9] + LD[13] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[3] + LD[6] + LD[10] + LD[14] + LD[17] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[7] + LD[11] + LD[15] + LD[18] = MAGIC_SUM,
LD[12] + LD[16] + LD[19] = MAGIC_SUM
